    "created_at": "2020-07-20T18:56:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-07-20T18:56:45Z",
    "body": "By autofill do you mean a value for the autocomplete attribute? Like `<input autocomplete=\"citizen-id\">`? Or would it look like `<input autocomplete=on name=\"citizen-id\">`?\r\nI'm not super familiar with this feature, I never knew about the autocomplete attribute before this discussion.\r\n\r\nThis was started [in a chrome bug](https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=1106924) which also has a bunch of discussion. I am hoping we can come to a decision in this issue.\r\n\r\nBased on the discussion here it sounds like there are several requests and possible solutions:\r\n- Autofill\r\nIt sounds like adding a new autofill field solves this\r\n- Determining appropriate input type on phones\r\n`inputmode=numeric` can be used to solve this when the id is supposed to be a number.\r\n- Accessibility\r\nWhat exactly is wrong with the current accessibility?\r\n- Password management\r\nI don't know how these things work, but if they are looking for an input type, then they could also look for autocomplete and related attributes, right?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
